      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is an extremely important feature.\n\nWe recognize that VRChat Groups are the most suitable system for hosting events, with many of them utilizing group instances.\n\nThe feature for performers and staff to reliably join these instances is highly desired, as it often helps reduce the burden of event management.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "6751672b3f97e66062039779",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "5c8ff1b1f7d44e7de9d0203d",
        "alias": "Olive drab Whippet",
        "aliasID": "65c2a286ed6eefce4c72d2bc",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/25c0f533f2624723ab1ea1256e7cbb0e.png",
        "created": "2019-03-18T19:29:53.906Z",
        "name": "FloydianSound",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "sam-floyd"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2024-12-05T08:41:15.528Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "67219e9c228d65cb8e5d14ef",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Users who disconnect involuntarily should have a grace period (5minutes ?) to rejoin the world they were in previously, even at the cost of overpopulation. \n\nSome apps like VRCX allows to rejoin the same lobby after a crash; but if the lobby already is full, you'll end up in a new, different lobby... and you gotta wait for the queue again.\n\nThere are already VIP spots in lobby queues being sold for real money... i don't think it should be a stretch to let ANY users who waited and earn their spot to reconnect if they didn't disconnect on their own actions (aka, they crashed...).\n\nThis is especially important for performers (like myself) and group moderators (most of my friends). \n\nConsidering the history of crashing and Griefing; you can guess that's its a still problematic still to this day, too. The burden falls on said group moderators to scramble a solution to get the performer back in the lobby ASAP, sometimes at the expense of kicking someone already present (with whatever trust ranking score, and time lost consequences). \n\nit's kinda shitty but it still does happens. \n\nnot even later than last week i saw a whole lobby dropped connection at once.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "6850616aa769985a0f54b11b",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "672e245794da76013c4042fc",
        "alias": "Marvellous Grouse",
        "aliasID": "672e2458c66e81bbd4e46364",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/e7953757401aa0362d8c77239fff010e.png",
        "created": "2024-11-08T14:46:47.792Z",
        "name": "Verhs",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "verhs"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2025-06-16T18:24:42.834Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "67219e9c228d65cb8e5d14ef",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 6
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To build on this and provide a slightly alternative take..\n\nVRChat has no real support for events at present. Presently Performers and staff take up valuable slots for attendees. This means that:\n\n- The more staff present at an event, the less potential attendee engagement there is\n\n- Events become limited due to needing to sacrifice performer/staff numbers to maximize attendee engagement\n\n- There is no way to swap out performers and staff (say, due to technical problems) without the replacement staff member having to wait in the instance queue which can completely derail an event\n\nEffectively, the current system limits potential quality of events and attendee safety because there is no way to prioritize staff members.\n\nTo remedy this, there should be a way to designate a “Staff Group” for an instance that allows for somewhere around 18 members of event staff (18 would well-suit some of the actor/staff-heavy events perfectly, esp. those that need actors, media teams, security, administrative organizers, and technical support) to join and leave the instance in their own separate slots/queue (E.g. 80 attendees, 18 staff, totaling a maximum of 98 people). This would allow for events to maximize attendee engagement and attendee safety, as well as to provide them the ability to handle technical issues without events being derailed.\n\nI’d see this playing out where:\n\n- The staff numbers for events to be listed in yellow/orange beside the current instance population.\n\n- Event Staff would join this queue by having the associated group active in their profile, and then when joining the event instance/s be presented with an option of taking up a normal slot or a staff slot only when that Staff Group is active\n\nTo note: This is different from priority queueing in that this is not for potential monetization. This is for attendee engagement, safety, and the allowance of smooth event operations which is core to the event community at large.\n\nThis is also something that would pair well with a *separate* feature that allows for event/instance creators to specify world population limits.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
